  "notes": [
    "Research overlay only; persistent Shipyard SQLite is never replaced by this package.",
    "The GLB visual library stores complete GLB BLOBs plus catalog metadata inside the existing Shipyard design-ledger SQLite.",
    "GOVERNED_SEMANTIC, VISUAL_REFERENCE, and EXTERNAL_FIXTURE assets remain authority-distinct; visual-reference and fixture assets never gain engineering authority.",
    "The Pixel library viewer prefers WebGL2 and explicitly enables OES_element_index_uint on WebGL1 so legacy visual-reference GLBs using UNSIGNED_INT index accessors can render without rewriting their stored bytes.",
    "The current governed semantic Wayfarer remains generated from Design State and stored as a library member; imported Wayfarer visual-reference GLBs are preserved byte-for-byte as non-authoritative visual references.",
    "Component-level GLB decomposition remains deferred until library, visualization, and image-realization acceptance are closed."
